7}],"shots":[{"focus":["dig","crosswalk","streetSign"],"width":0.85}]},{"s":"congrats","shows":{"p":"bigPipe","does":"a calm street over the finished drain"},"do":[],"shots":[{"focus":"home","type":"wide"}]}],"audio":{"cards":[{"text":"600 GALLONS","at":{"s":"problem","w":"600"},"d":1.8},{"text":"27,000 GALLONS","at":{"s":"fact","w":"over"},"d":1.8},{"text":"6X THE WATER","at":{"s":"factProof","w":"six"},"d":1.8}],"sfx":[{"lib":"dirt","at":{"s":"hook","w":"dig","o":0.3},"d":1.4},{"lib":"drip","at":{"s":"problem","w":"gallons"},"d":1.3},{"lib":"water_rush","at":{"s":"how","w":"rushes"},"d":1.6},{"lib":"water_rush","at":{"s":"problem3","w":"bursts"},"d":1.6},{"lib":"water_rush","at":{"s":"name2","w":"outfall"},"d":1.4}],"chimes":[{"s":"problem","w":"600"},{"s":"name"},{"s":"fact","w":"over"},{"s":"factProof","w":"six"},{"s":"name2"},{"s":"congrats"}],"rain":{"from":{"s":"problem","w":"rain"},"to":{"s":"finish","w":"Add"},"underDb":24}},"codeShots":true,"why":"A street corner in section: a hole by the curb floods in the rain, a pipe drains it, leaves clog it until a grate covers it, a parking lot overloads it until a bigger pipe goes in, and the outfall shows where the water really goes. The camera opens close on the dug hole, frames each fix and failure at street level, goes low for the pipes and the creek, and ends on a calm wide street.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you dig a hole by the curb, you have a ditch."},{"role":"problem","text":"But one inch of rain on a driveway makes roughly 600 gallons that trickle into the street."},{"role":"flood","text":"The water has nowhere to go, so the dead end floods the street."},{"role":"stakes","text":"It rises to the top of the curb, right at the shop doors."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you lay a pipe under the street, and the water drains away."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now leaves wash into the open pipe and clog it, so the street fills again."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a grate over the opening to keep them out."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a storm drain."},{"role":"how","text":"Rain drops through the grate and rushes down the pipe."},{"role":"fix3","text":"So you hook a parking lot up to the drain too."},{"role":"fact","text":"One acre of parking lot makes over 27,000 gallons in an inch of rain."},{"role":"problem3","text":"But now the pipe is too small, so water bursts up through the grate and floods over the curb."},{"role":"fix4","text":"So you lay a bigger pipe, twice as wide."},{"role":"factProof","text":"A pipe twice as wide carries about six times as much water."},{"role":"name2","text":"This is an outfall, where the pipe empties into a creek."},{"role":"myth","text":"And this water is not cleaned at a treatment plant."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"It pours untreated into the creek, and the creek turns brown."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add crosswalk stripes and a street sign."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a storm drain."}]}